  <context description="Mastra framework development considerations">
    Mastra is a TypeScript framework for building AI-powered applications with agents, workflows, and tools. It provides production-ready infrastructure with observability, memory management, and deployment capabilities.

    Key architectural principles:
    - TypeScript-first with ES2022 modules and bundler resolution
    - Agents as autonomous reasoning entities with LLM and tool integration
    - Workflows as graph-based orchestration for explicit control
    - Tools as structured operations with Zod schemas
    - Hono-based HTTP server for production deployment
    - Memory management with thread and resource scoping
    - Multi-provider support (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, 40+ providers)

    Production considerations:
    - Use `mastra build` to generate Hono server
    - Configure CORS for cross-origin requests
    - Set appropriate timeouts and body limits
    - Implement structured output with Zod for reliability
    - Use streaming for long-running responses
    - Monitor token usage and costs
    - Implement proper error handling and logging

    Best practices from Mastra.ai team:
    - Register agents in Mastra instance for shared resources
    - Use memory with thread/resource IDs for conversation context
    - Implement onStepFinish callbacks for monitoring
    - Use structured output instead of JSON parsing
    - Compose agents as workflow steps when possible
    - Use runtime context for dynamic configuration
    - Test agents with Mastra Studio before deployment
  </context>

